		(property "I2C_Address" "0x20"
			(at 0 0 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
		(property "Note" "FBV2-S1-008: TCA9535PWR -> NXP PCAL9535APW,118. PIN-TO-PIN IDENTICAL - NXP data sheet Rev. 2, 23-Jan-2015 calls the part a pin-to-pin replacement for the PCA9535 and the TSSOP24 pinning matches the inherited symbol exactly, so no wire moved. Address 0 1 0 0 A2 A1 A0. THE SWAP IS NOT COSMETIC, and it is what makes this sheet work: (1) programmable 100 k pull-up/pull-down per bit (46h/47h enable, 48h/49h select) so RESERVED and unused pins need no external resistors, which the TCA9535 cannot do; (2) an interrupt MASK (4Ah/4Bh) and a read-only interrupt STATUS register (4Ch/4Dh) that names the changed input, where the TCA9535 forces firmware to read every port of both devices and still cannot tell which bit moved; (3) all interrupts MASKED at power-up, so bring-up is free of spurious INT; (4) four output drive strengths (40h-43h) to slow edges for EMI. POWER-UP REGISTER STATE THAT THE SAFE-STATE ANALYSIS DEPENDS ON: Configuration 06h/07h = FFh (all pins high-impedance INPUTS); Output port 02h/03h = FFh, so a pin DRIVES HIGH the instant firmware makes it an output; pull-up/pull-down enable 46h/47h = 00h, so the internal resistors are OFF and the only current at a high-Z pin is the 1 uA IIH/IIL leakage limit. FIRMWARE CONTRACT: write the Output port register BEFORE the Configuration register, or the five active-low resets and AMP_SD_MODE will glitch to their inactive state on the write that makes them outputs. Outputs sink 25 mA each for direct LED drive; abs max 50 mA per I/O, 200 mA ISS, 200 mW Ptot. Standby 1.0 uA typ at 3.3 V."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
