	(text "BUTTONS - MIGRATED FBV2-S1-008\n\nSIX BUTTONS: UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT, A/SELECT, B/BACK.\nHOME (SW8) AND ITS PULL-UP R10 ARE REMOVED - THE SIX-BUTTON\nSET IS THE LOCKED ONE. VOLUME BUTTONS NEVER EXISTED\nELECTRICALLY AND ARE NOT INVENTED HERE.\n\nACTIVE LOW: 10 k EXTERNAL PULL-UP TO +3V3, SWITCH TO GND.\nTHE PULL-UPS STAY EXTERNAL EVEN THOUGH THE PCAL9535A HAS\nINTERNAL 100 k ONES - 100 k WITH THE PCAL 1 uA LEAKAGE AND\nPCB CONTAMINATION IS A WEAK HIGH, AND AN EXTERNAL 10 k IS\nDEFINED BEFORE FIRMWARE HAS WRITTEN A SINGLE REGISTER.\nSTEADY CURRENT WHEN A BUTTON IS HELD: 0.33 mA.\n\nNO RC DEBOUNCE. THE PTS645 BOUNCES <= 5 ms AND THE INPUT IS\nREAD OVER I2C AFTER AN INTERRUPT - HUNDREDS OF MICROSECONDS\nOF LATENCY ALREADY - SO A CAPACITOR WOULD ADD PARTS AND\nSOLVE NOTHING. DEBOUNCE IN FIRMWARE. THE PCAL INPUT LATCH\n(44h/45h) IS AVAILABLE IF A SHORT PRESS IS EVER MISSED."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 245.11 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fb080008-0808-4808-9808-000000000014")
	)

