		(property "Note" "BQ25185 STAT1 pull-up, FBV2-S1-008. SLUSF65A Table 5-1: STAT1 and STAT2 are OPEN-DRAIN, pull-up resistor 1 kOhm to 20 kOhm, maximum pull-up rail 5 V, 20 mA sink, and either may be left floating if unused. 10 kOhm is inside that window and is chosen over the 20 kOhm of Ruling G for the same reason the button pull-ups are 10 kOhm and not the PCAL internal 100 kOhm: the expander input leaks up to 1 uA and the board will be handled, so a stiffer high is worth 0.33 mA - and that current only flows while the charger is actually holding the pin LOW. CHARGER STATE DECODE, SLUSF65A Table 7-2: STAT1 LOW = charging; STAT1 HIGH with STAT2 LOW = fault; both HIGH is ONE combined state covering charge complete, sleep and charge disabled. WITH NO BATTERY FITTED the device cycles the BAT-pin capacitor and STAT2 TOGGLES while STAT1 stays stable - which is why both pins are landed, and why firmware must leave the STAT2 interrupt mask bit SET and poll instead."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
		(pin "1"
			(uuid "fb080108-0801-4b08-9b08-000000000004")
		)
		(pin "2"
			(uuid "fb080108-0801-4b08-9b08-000000000005")
