				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
		(property "Note" "ACC_DETECT_N pull-up, FBV2-S1-008. D-085 locks the convention: the accessory asserts detect by shorting community-port pin 23 to the adjacent GND at pin 21 with ONE 0 Ohm link, and AQROOT provides the 100 kOhm pull-up to +3V3. The pull-up and the expander both run from +3V3, so DETECTION WORKS WITH BOTH ACCESSORY RAILS OFF - which is what makes MX-3 implementable (neither rail may be enabled unless ACC_DETECT_N is asserted) and what makes a flipped accessory passively safe: it cannot ground pin 23, so it never receives power. THE RESISTOR IS PLACED HERE, AT THE EXPANDER, rather than on sheet 09, so the input has a defined level before the connector sheet is migrated. SHEET 09 MUST NOT ADD A SECOND PULL-UP - it adds only the connector contact to this same net."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
