	(text "U2 INTERNAL EXPANDER - MIGRATED FBV2-S1-008\nNXP PCAL9535APW,118   I2C ADDRESS 0x20\nA0 = A1 = A2 = GND\n\nPORT 0 = P00-P04 OUT, P05-P07 IN  (06h = E0h)\nPORT 1 = 8 INPUTS                 (07h = FFh)\n16 / 16 USED - ZERO SPARE\n\nP00 TOUCH_RST_N       OUT  ACTIVE LOW\nP01 SX1262_RST_N      OUT  ACTIVE LOW\nP02 NFC_5V_EN         OUT  ACTIVE HIGH\nP03 AMP_SD_MODE       OUT  ACTIVE HIGH\nP04 DISP_RST_N        OUT  ACTIVE LOW\nP05 BQ25185_STAT1     IN   R127 10k UP\nP06 BQ25185_STAT2     IN   R128 10k UP\nP07 SD_CARD_DETECT_N  IN   R113 100k UP, SHEET 03\nP10-P13 D-PAD UP/DOWN/LEFT/RIGHT  IN  10k UP\nP14 BTN_A_N   P15 BTN_B_N         IN  10k UP\nP16 TOUCH_INT_N       IN   FT6236, ACTIVE LOW\nP17 SX1262_DIO1       IN   ACTIVE HIGH\n\nEVERY P05-P17 INPUT IS INTERRUPT-CAPABLE AND EVERY\nONE POWERS UP MASKED (4Ah/4Bh = FFh). FIRMWARE\nUNMASKS THE SIX BUTTONS, TOUCH_INT_N, SX1262_DIO1\nAND SD_CARD_DETECT_N, AND LEAVES BQ25185_STAT2\nMASKED - IT TOGGLES CONTINUOUSLY WHEN NO BATTERY IS\nFITTED AND WOULD OTHERWISE WAKE THE MCU FOREVER."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 82.804 33.782 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "fb080108-0801-4b08-9b08-00000000007a")
	)

	(text "U3 COMMUNITY EXPANDER - MIGRATED FBV2-S1-008\nNXP PCAL9535APW,118   I2C ADDRESS 0x21\nA0 = +3V3, A1 = A2 = GND\n\nP00 FRONT_RGB_R_N     INTERNAL RGB SINK\nP01 FRONT_RGB_G_N     INTERNAL RGB SINK\nP02 FRONT_RGB_B_N     INTERNAL RGB SINK\nP03 ACC_5V_SW_EN      OUT, R131 100k DOWN, SHEET 01\nP04-P05 XGPIO4-5      COMMUNITY, BIDIRECTIONAL\nP06-P07, P10-P11      UNUSED, NC-DEMO\nP12 ACC_3V3_EN        OUT  R98 100k DOWN, SHEET 01\nP13 ACC_5V_BOOST_EN   OUT  R102 100k DOWN, SHEET 01\nP14 ACC_DETECT_N      IN   R129 100k UP, HERE\nP15 ACC_POWER_FAULT_N IN   R103 100k UP, SHEET 01\nP16 SX1262_RXEN       OUT  R74 PULL-DOWN, SHEET 04\nP17 ACC_PWR_EN        OUT  R17 100k DOWN, HERE\n12 / 16 USED - FOUR NC-DEMO CHANNELS\n\nXGPIO10-13 ARE RETIRED - THE PORT IS LOCKED AT TEN\nXGPIO (D-082). SHEET 09 STILL CARRIES THE FOUR OLD\nHEADER PINS AND THEY DANGLE UNTIL IT MIGRATES.\n\nACC_PWR_EN IS INHERITED, NOT DESIGNED. IT DRIVES\nONLY U15 AND U16, WHICH ARE BOTH DNP, AND IT IS THE\nPIN THE SHEET-09 O-4 RULING MAY RETIRE. IT IS KEPT\nBECAUSE REMOVING IT WOULD LEAVE TWO SHEET-09 INPUTS\nUNDRIVEN, AND SHEET 09 IS OUT OF SCOPE HERE.\n\nMX-9: U3 XGPIO INTERRUPTS ARE MASKED BY DEFAULT SO\nAN ACCESSORY CANNOT HOLD THE SHARED WAKE LINE AND\nSTARVE THE BUTTONS. ONLY ACC_DETECT_N AND\nACC_POWER_FAULT_N ARE UNMASKED.\n\nAQROOT DEMO ECO: P13 ENABLES THE TPS61023 BOOST; P03\nSEPARATELY ENABLES THE TPS22950C LOAD SWITCH. THE TWO\n5 V CONTROLS REMAIN INDEPENDENT WITH SAFE-STATE PULLS."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 168.402 33.274 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "fb080108-0801-4b08-9b08-00000000007b")
	)

	(text "FRONT RGB STATUS LIGHT - IMPLEMENTED FBV2-S1-008\n\nD13 = MEIHUA MHPA3528RGBCT  (LCSC C409779)\n  COMMON ANODE, SMD3528-4P 3.5 x 2.8 x 1.85 mm,\n  120 deg, WATER CLEAR, 69k IN STOCK, $0.084/2k.\n  PIN 1 = A, 2 = BLUE K, 3 = GREEN K, 4 = RED K.\n  NOTE THIS IS **NOT** Device:LED_ARGB ORDER\n  (THAT SYMBOL HAS 2 = RED, 4 = BLUE).\n\nTHREE RESISTORS, CALCULATED SEPARATELY FROM THE\nLOW-CURRENT Fig.4 CURVES - THE TABULATED VF IS\nQUOTED AT 20 mA AND IS USELESS AT 1-2 mA:\n\n        VF      R      NOM     HIGH    LOW\n  RED   1.75  1k00   1.50mA  1.70mA  1.18mA\n  GRN   2.55   680   1.03mA  1.32mA  0.57mA\n  BLU   2.60   390   1.67mA  2.17mA  0.86mA\n  WHITE            4.20mA  5.18mA  2.60mA\n\nCORNERS = 3.234/3.366 V RAIL, VF SPREAD, VOL\n0.02-0.10 V. BLUE GETS THE MOST CURRENT AND RED\nTHE LEAST BECAUSE Iv AT 20 mA IS R 1070 / G 1685\n/ B 500 mcd TYP; THE RESULT IS ~80 / 87 / 42 mcd.\n\nNO TRANSISTORS, NO DRIVER IC, NO EXTRA RAIL.\nTHE PCAL9535A SINKS 25 mA PER PIN FOR DIRECT LED\nDRIVE (ABS MAX 50 mA/PIN, 200 mA ISS, 200 mW).\nWORST PIN IS 2.17 mA = 11x MARGIN; THE PACKAGE\nSEES 5.2 mA = 38x MARGIN AND ~0.35 mW.\n\nSAFE STATE - THE ACTUAL CIRCUIT ANALYSIS:\n  POWER-UP  CONFIG 06h = FFh -> PIN IS HIGH-Z,\n            PULL ENABLE 46h = 00h -> INTERNAL\n            100k IS **OFF**, SO THE ONLY CURRENT\n            IS THE 1 uA IIH/IIL LEAKAGE LIMIT\n            = ~0.05 mcd = INVISIBLE.\n  TRANSITION OUTPUT PORT 02h = FFh, SO THE PIN\n            DRIVES **HIGH** THE INSTANT IT\n            BECOMES AN OUTPUT. NO GLITCH.\n  THEREFORE NO EXTERNAL PULL-UP IS NEEDED ON ANY\n  CATHODE NODE. ADDING ONE WOULD BE THREE PARTS\n  THAT DO NOTHING.\n\nESD: GREEN AND BLUE ARE ONLY 150 V HBM (RED IS\n2000 V). TREAT D13 AS ESD SENSITIVE IN ASSEMBLY.\n\nTHE THREE SINKS ARE U3 P00/P01/P02 FOR AQROOT DEMO.\nTHE RETIRED PUBLIC XGPIO0-2 CHANNELS ARE REUSED INTERNALLY.\n\nFRONT-FACING BY REQUIREMENT, EXACT POSITION NOT\nLOCKED: UPPER BEZEL, LOWER BEZEL, BESIDE THE DISPLAY\nOR NEAR THE CONTROLS ARE ALL ACCEPTABLE. IT IS NOT\nA TOP-EDGE PART. IT MUST SIT BEHIND A DIFFUSER OR\nLIGHT PIPE - NO PROTRUDING BARE LED. PLACEMENT AND\nCAD OWN THE FINAL POSITION."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 223.52 116.332 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "fb080108-0801-4b08-9b08-00000000007c")
	)

	

	(text "EXPANDER INTERRUPTS - FBV2-S1-008\n\nBOTH /INT PINS ARE OPEN-DRAIN AND WIRE-OR ONTO\nWAKE_INT_N, WHICH R3 10 k PULLS TO +3V3 AND WHICH REACHES\nGPIO21. THE PULL-UP IS MANDATORY - THE DATA SHEET SAYS SO -\nAND IT IS WHAT MAKES THE LINE DETERMINISTIC (INACTIVE HIGH)\nBEFORE ANY REGISTER IS WRITTEN. GPIO21 IS NOT A STRAPPING\nPIN, SO A HELD INTERRUPT CANNOT BLOCK ROM DOWNLOAD.\n\nPCAL9535A POWERS UP WITH **ALL INTERRUPTS MASKED**\n(4Ah/4Bh = FFh), SO BRING-UP IS FREE OF SPURIOUS INT AND\nFIRMWARE UNMASKS ONLY WHAT IT WANTS. THE READ-ONLY STATUS\nREGISTERS 4Ch/4Dh - WHICH THE TCA9535 DOES NOT HAVE - NAME\nTHE CHANGED BIT DIRECTLY INSTEAD OF FORCING A READ OF EVERY\nPORT REGISTER ON EVERY DEVICE.\n\nDISCOVERY ORDER ON A WAKE: READ 4Ch/4Dh ON U2, THEN ON U3.\nINT CLEARS ON A READ OF THE INPUT PORT REGISTER, SO FIRMWARE\nMUST READ 00h/01h AFTER THE STATUS REGISTER OR THE LINE\nSTAYS LOW AND NO FURTHER EDGE IS SEEN.\n\nMASK POLICY. UNMASKED: THE SIX BUTTONS, TOUCH_INT_N,\nSX1262_DIO1, SD_CARD_DETECT_N ON U2; ACC_DETECT_N AND\nACC_POWER_FAULT_N ON U3. MASKED: BQ25185_STAT2, WHICH\nTOGGLES FOREVER WITH NO BATTERY FITTED, AND THE TWO RETAINED XGPIO,\nWHICH IS MX-9 - AN ACCESSORY MUST NOT BE ABLE TO HOLD THE\nSHARED WAKE LINE AND STARVE THE BUTTONS.\n\nTHE INPUT LATCH (44h/45h) IS AVAILABLE IF A SHORT PRESS IS\nEVER MISSED BETWEEN THE INTERRUPT AND THE I2C READ."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.9 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "fb080108-0801-4b08-9b08-0000000dbba1")
	)

	

	

)
